WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.560
- All right, we gotta talk about these

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.400
folding phones for a minute,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.860
because it's changed a lot
since the last time we did.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.650
So the first ever folding
phone from OnePlus

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.640
came out this week.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.886
It's called the OnePlus Open.

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:12.210
Not a very good name,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.670
but a very, very, very good,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.720
first gen foldable.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.610
I've been using it for
about three weeks now.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.050
I got lots of good things to say about it,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.000
but it's actually, I
feel like it's so good,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.880
that it's actually resurfaced
the old question in my head

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.070
from a couple years ago, which is,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.810
what's it gonna take for regular people

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.210
to actually start buying folding phones?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.010
Because, yeah, I like this phone,

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.570
and I'm gonna go ahead and guess that

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.060
some other reviewers
will like this phone too,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.100
and some enthusiasts will like this phone,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.470
and this video may even
get a lot of views,

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.470
but none of that necessarily translates

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.290
into regular people just
like, strolling into a store,

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.740
or going online and choosing
to buy one of these.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.720
So first things first,
the details of this phone.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.710
So this is a super high-end
phone in every way,

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.380
and the design is
particularly well considered.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.750
You can see it's basically the same size

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.163
as a normal phone on the outside.

00:01:02.163 --> 00:01:06.150
This is a 6.3 inch, 20
by nine cover display,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.410
just over 1080p.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.600
It's LTPO down to 10 hertz,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.600
and it's an absurdly bright
2800 nits max brightness

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.440
between these pretty thin bezels.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.030
So this actually does take the crown now

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.660
for the brightest display I
have ever seen in a smartphone.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.510
And I'm gonna go ahead
and give it the co-crown

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.690
for best foldable to use while closed,

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.250
alongside the Pixel Fold.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.050
So I still think the Pixel Fold has,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.030
it's more reachable, it has
better button placement,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.440
since it's a bit shorter.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.110
But there's no question this
feels like a flagship phone

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.080
on the outside, even if you
never even open the thing.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.540
There's also a bunch of
design touches I really like,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.480
the flat sides all the
way around, super clean.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.490
The alert slider is also back,

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.650
so it's way up there at
the top of the phone,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.670
which is kind of tough to reach,

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.400
but I love that it works
exactly as you'd expect.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.310
Same as previous OnePlus
phones that had it.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.560
And the power button also doubles
as the fingerprint reader,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.750
which we've seen with lots
of these folds as well.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.583
It's awesome.

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.060
And then around the back,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.500
mixed bag, I would say.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.880
I'm not the biggest fake leather

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.080
on the back of a phone person.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.061
It gives me like, Samsung 2016 vibes,

00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:11.940
but at least it does hide fingerprints.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:12.930
This is the other color now.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.340
It's a green.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.330
It looks a little bit cleaner.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.060
But really, the feature is
the gigantic camera bump.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.650
And yeah, it's pretty crazy looking,

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.020
but, but, it also happens to be

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.608
exactly where my index finger rests

00:02:23.608 --> 00:02:25.530
on the back of the phone.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.300
So it's like a nice little shelf

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.330
that feels really natural when
using the phone while closed.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.550
So I kind of really like it for that.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.930
Also, the LED flash.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:34.920
I guess it couldn't fit,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.170
so they shoved it up in the
corner, for some reason.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.850
But, then you open this thing up,

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.533
and it just, it becomes so
obvious why they waited so long

00:02:41.533 --> 00:02:43.350
to do their first foldable.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.840
It looks nothing like some of the other

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.630
first gen folding screens from years ago.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.480
It's got this huge 7.8
inch corner to corner,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.360
LTPO 3.0 display, that again,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.290
goes up to 2800 nits,
and down to one hertz.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.790
Even bezels all the way around,

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.230
got the hole punch in the top corner.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.930
And honestly, one of the
least visible creases

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.210
you will see in a folding phone in 2023.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.310
Now I think it's actually debatable

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.010
if we can technically call this
their first foldable phone,

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.779
because while OnePlus
hasn't made a foldable yet,

00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:16.740
their sister company, OPPO, clearly has.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.790
So I wouldn't be surprised

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.290
if this took a lot of tech from them.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.080
Actually, there is another
just released OPPO phone

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.830
called the OPPO Find N3,
and it's the same as this,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.730
but the point still stands.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.780
And with this screen on,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.084
you literally don't see the
crease at all, and screen off,

00:03:31.084 --> 00:03:33.030
you still kind of have to look for it.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:33.863
And then, yeah,

00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:35.010
you hit the angle where the light reflects

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.840
off of the middle of the
phone, and then you can see it.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.460
But this is one of those phones that

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.440
looks really good from almost every angle

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.820
you would actually use it.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.290
And then it also has one of those hinges

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.834
that stays at whatever
angle that you hold it at.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:48.291
So if you want a sort
of a 90 degree angle,

00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:50.970
or a little bit more open
or closed, you can do that.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:54.840
And then it has a nice satisfying
spring loaded clap shut.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.280
It's also, it's impressively thin.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.950
It's not the thinnest one I've
ever seen, but pretty good.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.450
It's lighter than you would expect.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.070
It's actually, if you put it on a scale,

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.648
it's basically the exact same
weight as an iPhone 14 Pro

00:04:04.648 --> 00:04:06.300
when they're doing stainless steel.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.130
So, just a regular phone weight.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.270
So it's an impressive piece of hardware.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.480
But then the software
for this one is OnePlus.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.790
So it's OxygenOS 13.2,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.640
and it's got all kinds of little
tweaks and little features

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.740
that power users are gonna love.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.950
Because let's face it, this
is a phone for power users.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.240
People who are gonna love the

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.520
continuity features
between the open screen

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.510
and the closed screen.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.100
So once you're done using a big app,

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.450
you just close it like this,

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.820
and then swipe up to pick
up where you left off

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.770
on the outside screen, if you want to.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.060
Just like the Pixel Fold,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.820
it's gonna mirror your home
screen set up automatically

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.980
between the cover screen
and the inside screen.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.180
So if you change something,

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.390
like move a folder or a
widget or an app on one,

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.590
and then switch to the other,

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.840
it will have also moved from there too.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.700
Keeps them a little bit more organized.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.380
I kind of wish I had the
option to change that,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.570
since this is Android,
and I am a power user.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.150
But nevertheless, that's the way it is.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.240
But then there's also a ton
of multitasking features

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.630
on the inside screen, for having
multiple apps open at once.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.550
So you can have, obviously,

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.930
one app open full screen,

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.850
and that looks good for a
surprising number of apps.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.460
It'll stretch them if they're
not natively built for this.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.700
But then you can have
two apps side by side,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.670
and then you can pick a
third app to get in the mix.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.410
Then they're all just
sort of next to each other

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.240
in this triple panel view,

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.980
and you can move things
between them really quickly.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.540
Or if you pinch out with four fingers,

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.930
you can see all of the apps at once.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.580
So between that and the dock,

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.740
with all of your apps and recent files,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.290
it's just a very well considered hub for

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.570
sitting down and just getting stuff done.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.184
Like I feel like when I sit
down and open this phone,

00:05:38.184 --> 00:05:41.250
I'm about to be really
productive and get a lot done.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.720
This phone, the OnePlus Open,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.190
honestly, as a phone,

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.820
it nails all five of my
pillars of a great smartphone.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.260
Great screen, great battery,

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:50.790
great build, great performance,

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.970
great camera, and I'm not
being generous with that stuff.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.080
It like, actually nails all of that stuff.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.460
Like you already heard
about the great screen,

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.470
and the fact that they
match each other so well

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:01.020
inside and outside, is
already pretty great.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.700
There's also great performance.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:03.900
Super high-end specs.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.250
Snapdragon 8 gen 2, 16 gigs of fast RAM,

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.520
512 gigs of UFS 4.0 storage.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.830
I mean the pair of 120 hertz LTPO displays

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.290
have a 240 hertz touch sample rate.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.120
It's super responsive, and I mean,

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.920
the whole thing feels very future-proof.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.480
And then you also heard
about the build quality,

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.400
which I'll revisit that in a second.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.218
But then battery life
has also been excellent,

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:28.050
with this 4800 MilliAmp hour battery,

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.140
and 67 watt fast charging,

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.710
although it just skips wireless
charging, for some reason,

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.796
which is like the most OnePlus thing ever.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.790
I think it adds like,

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.370
no cost and no weight and no thickness,

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.420
but yet they leave it out

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.580
when all the other
competitors have it anyway?

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:45.420
Alright, fine.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.580
But then this huge
camera module on the back

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.440
kind of implies high end cameras,

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.630
but you can never really be
sure until you test them.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:54.720
And sure enough, this
(indistinct) camera setup

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.100
is pretty decent.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.590
It's got this new stacked
sensor for the primary sensor,

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:01.140
a 3x telephoto, and an ultra wide.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.510
I found it's pretty good most of the time,

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.850
although it's not very
good at freezing motion.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:08.520
Which is fine if you take
photos of still subjects,

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.950
but the second it's people or animals,

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.560
and those things start to move,

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.580
then it can be kind of hard

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.830
getting a shutter speed fast
enough to freeze that stuff.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.260
You basically have to
switch to action mode,

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.460
which there's a button for.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.200
And that works by
cranking the shutter speed

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.190
way up, as expected,

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.710
but then ISO starts to get a little high,

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.660
high enough that photos
are now a little noisier,

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.560
a little worse looking,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.210
so it's just, that's unfortunate.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.040
And by the way, this isn't
one of the five pillars,

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.940
but I also found that the
microphone on this phone

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.770
is actually quite good.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.240
They're usually not this good.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.170
I was pleasantly surprised.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.170
But it all comes together
in a really nice phone

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.670
that I think a lot of
people including myself

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.410
are gonna really like using.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:48.030
So the question is,

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.520
why do I think people aren't buying

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.040
folding phones that much,
if they're this good?

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.560
It turns out, a phone
can hit all five pillars

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:56.393
of a great smartphone,

00:07:56.393 --> 00:08:00.420
and not be a great buy
for everyone, necessarily.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.340
And so it really comes down
to three things, I think.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.680
Number one is still price.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.500
Number two is the durability question.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.350
And then number three is
just the power user problem.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:15.350
So on price, this phone is $1700 US.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.490
That is a lot of money
to spend on a phone,

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.341
no matter how you chop it
up into monthly segments

00:08:19.341 --> 00:08:20.520
or staggered payments.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.510
It's just a lot, right?

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.880
It's literally twice as
much as an iPhone 15.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:24.713
But guess what?

00:08:24.713 --> 00:08:26.733
That's literally right in line
with its folding competitors,

00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:29.490
like the other two folding
phones available in the US,

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.800
Pixel Fold, $1800.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.560
Samsung Z Fold 5. $1800.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.390
So this one's actually kind of a bargain.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.580
That's the most obvious
thing holding these back,

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.350
'cause they're still so expensive.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.220
But then number two,

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.970
durability is also questionable at best.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:47.790
Now of course, they do all
the testing that they can,

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:48.690
and guess what?

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.750
They've got IPX4 water
resistance, which is nice.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.100
And they have a durability rating

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.730
for a million folds of the
hinge, and that's great.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.860
But then, what about these dead pixels

00:08:58.860 --> 00:08:59.880
that have started appearing

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.560
at the bottom middle of my screen,

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.180
right around the hinge?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.120
I had this one for three
weeks, and babied it,

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.160
and this is already
starting to show up on mine.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.690
It doesn't mean it's
gonna be bad for everyone,

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.310
but that's not great,

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:14.460
and I suspect it's not gonna
happen on non-folding phones.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:17.310
But the third and final
reason folding phones,

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.020
as great as they've been getting,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.260
aren't necessarily translating
to mainstream success,

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.810
is that they're power user phones.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:28.590
They're, folding and unfolding
is a power user feature.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:32.130
And power user features,
as much as we love 'em,

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.510
don't sell a ton of phones.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.310
We figured this out many times

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.935
when LG spent years and years

00:09:36.935 --> 00:09:39.210
making some of the most
manually adjustable cameras

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.220
in the smartphone world,

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.630
and now they don't make
smartphones anymore.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:43.650
And we still have Sony,

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:45.750
who can't stop making professional cameras

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:46.950
in a smartphone body,

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.810
but their sales are putting them

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.550
in danger of the same thing.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:54.180
And Asus ZenFones are
absolutely incredible right now,

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.920
for enthusiasts like myself,

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.840
but they've already thrown a head fake.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.480
Clearly they're not
doing super well either.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.740
I'd honestly be willing to bet,

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.110
without even being able to
look into anyone's books,

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:08.370
that the folding phones
are not at the top of sales

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.770
in any of the lineups
of any of the companies

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:11.760
who are making these things.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:14.610
Probably the most compelling
folding phone hardware

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:16.830
I've seen yet, is this HONOR phone.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:20.310
This thing's called the HONOR Magic V2.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.600
Bro, look at this thing!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.190
This, it's super thin,

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.740
it has all the right things
in all the right places.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.904
It's got a 3D printed
titanium hinge cover,

00:10:27.904 --> 00:10:31.080
barely showing any crease when it's open.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.200
Thin bezels, nice screens
all the way around.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:37.230
Somehow it has a 5000
MilliAmp hour battery inside,

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.730
and high-end specs.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:41.970
Like, playing with this phone
over almost anything else,

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.500
over even Samsung's,

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.040
has helped me appreciate
what folding phone hardware

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.210
can actually be.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.590
But despite all that awesomeness,

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:52.050
it still has those kind
of obvious downsides

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.250
for a regular person,

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.800
to probably not pick it
over a regular phone.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.170
The price, it's like 1400 bucks.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.163
The durability?

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.580
Potentially compromised, we don't know.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.140
And then even though
it is thin and awesome,

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.250
it's still just like,

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.100
the power user thing of wanting to carry

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.240
a slightly thicker phone around

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.680
and have that extra ability

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.264
is not something everyone sees as obvious

00:11:13.264 --> 00:11:15.120
and something they actually want.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.500
We are starting to
finally see some of those

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.950
flipping phones come at least
closer to the mainstream,

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.050
because they are lower in price.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.770
The the Z Flip 5 is down to a
thousand bucks from Samsung.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:29.040
And Motorola just launched
their most affordable flip yet,

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.120
the Razr 40, I think is
launching soon at 600 bucks.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.670
So that seems to be getting
closer, but it's just,

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.740
we need a lot more of that stuff.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:41.490
So, folding phones are simultaneously

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:45.630
very evolved from their
beginnings just a few years ago,

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.483
and yet still have a long way to go.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:52.773
So I guess until we get there,
it's more fun for us nerds.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:54.673
Thanks for watching!

00:11:54.673 --> 00:11:56.220
Catch you in the next one.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.419
Peace.

00:11:57.419 --> 00:12:01.176
(chill beats and uplifting strings music)

